#### 3. Technical Findings
1. **Four Bytes Seen at `ycrcb put`**:
   * Pre-paint sentinel: `0x11223344`
   * Foreground colour: `0xaabbccdd`
   * Observed: `0x56e8857a` (Run 1), `0x38abc4e1` (Run 2)
   * Classification: **Neither**. Destination memory received host pseudo-random bytes generated by `buf[0..3] = random()`, neither matching the sentinel nor any permutation/packing of the source colour.
2. **Attribution Text**:
   * Captured transcript string: `[ put: color mode = 0xf0 ]` for YCRCB (`0xf0`), and `[ put: color mode = 0x50 ]` for reserved mode (`0x50`), confirming execution of the `horrible_getputpixel()` `default:` arm.
3. **Read vs. Assumed**:
   * **Read**: [`src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L308-L340) switches on `color_mode = mode & DE_MODE_TYPE_MASK` (mask `0xf0`). The `default:` arm calls `random()`, prints via `fatal()` (which returns without exit in [`src/core/debugmsg.c`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/core/debugmsg.c#L384)), and allows `cpu->memory_rw()` to write PRNG bytes to guest memory. [`src/core/main.c`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/core/main.c#L688-L692) seeds `random()` with PID and timestamp.
   * **Assumed vs Measured**: `random()` is seeded per process on startup, so raw values vary across distinct runs on HEAD (`0x56e8857a` vs `0x38abc4e1`). Post-fix, a declined store will leave the sentinel `0x11223344` intact and deterministic across all runs.
